मण्डलम् वाक्यविभाग ॥ ॰ vakyavibhaga — the port of crates/sadhana/src/parse.rs

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE SASSEMBLY INSTRUCTION READER, task D-002f1, doc 03 §8.
॰
॰ It takes what पदविभाग lexed — चिह्नककोश, one चिह्नक per token — and
॰ turns a daṇḍa-terminated sentence into an आज्ञा, a ॱॱ into a चिह्न, and
॰ a ॥ … ॥ into whatever its निर्देश means, filling a कार्यक्रम that
॰ सङ्केतन (D-002a) turns into an image.
॰
॰ ── ADR-0030 REMEDIATION, TASK `D-002h` — THIS FILE IS THE LAST ──
॰ Every other source in crates/sadhana-t1/src/ is remediated; encode.t1
॰ closed on the cycle before this one after thirteen bounded parts. This
॰ file arrived at 487 अ६४ and NOT ONE न६४, and it is taken in parts for
॰ the same reason encode.t1 was: each site's spelling is read off its
॰ twin in crates/sadhana/src/parse.rs, not guessed from its neighbour.
॰
॰ THE PART TAKEN FIRST IS THE LINE NUMBER — 14 sites, all fourteen
॰ moving, all fourteen visible to the census: पङ्क्ति in आज्ञा, दत्तम्,
॰ चिह्न, वाक्य and वाक्यदोष, रिक्तपङ्क्ति in कार्यक्रम, the same
॰ parameter in all five *योजनम् appenders, the module-level
॰ रिक्तपङ्क्तिः, वैश्विकपङ्क्तिः's answer and the binding filled from
॰ it. 487/0 -> 473/14; corpus ledger 550/0/828 -> 536/0/842, sum 1378.
॰
॰ ITS READING WAS MADE THREE FILES AGO AND ONLY THE SITES ARE NEW.
॰ parse.rs declares line: usize five times and bss_line: usize once;
॰ lex.t1 spells Token::line न६४, parse.t1 spells ParseError::line न६४,
॰ encode.t1 spells सङ्केतनदोष ॱ पङ्क्ति न६४. EIGHT call sites here were
॰ already handing a पदविभागॱचिह्नक ॱ पङ्क्ति — an न६४ — into an अ६४
॰ parameter, so this was a live cross-file disagreement and not a tidy-up.
॰
॰ WHAT WAS READ AND LEFT: जालपङ्क्तिः and जालपाठः's पङ्क्तिः. Same name,
॰ different quantity — a ROW INDEX into the ADR-0019 table this file's
॰ own prose says is unreachable until जालकोशः gets a registry row. It
॰ has no twin to read, so it waits for the cycle that ports the table.
॰
॰ THE HANDLE FOR THE NEXT UNIT: पङ्क्तिसीमा's three consumers. सीमा is
॰ bound at अ६४ from it in जालपङ्क्तिः and in both संरेख walkers, while
॰ samyojana.t1 binds the same call at न६४ — a producer-moved-consumer-
॰ did-not with a cross-FILE precedent to read it against.
॰
॰ ── WHY THIS FILE DID NOT EXIST ──
॰ For a week the D-002 chain called its second blocker "B-109/parse.t1".
॰ That was FALSE and D-002a2 measured it false. crates/sadhana-t1/src/
॰ parse.t1 is मण्डलम् व्याकर, the T1 LANGUAGE parser — घोषणा,
॰ व्याकरदोष — and it is a port of crates/sadhana/src/t1/parse.rs. The
॰ Sassembly instruction reader, crates/sadhana/src/parse.rs, 1422 lines,
॰ had never been ported at all. Two files named parse and one of them
॰ absent is exactly how a whole module goes missing for a week.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAME आज्ञा — THERE ARE NOW TWO, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE ──
॰ मध्यरूपॱआज्ञा is the IR instruction, the port of t1/ir.rs's Instruction:
॰ a tag, a value it defines, and operands that are मूल्याङ्क. वाक्यविभागॱ
॰ आज्ञा is THIS one, the port of parse.rs's Instruction: a registry family,
॰ a व्याप्ति, the type names written after the mnemonic, and कारक-marked
॰ operands. They are different records of different things and neither is
॰ convertible to the other without उत्सर्जन in between. आज्ञा is the
॰ attested word for instruction (spec/lexicon.src.tsv) and both earn it;
॰ the मण्डलम् is what tells them apart, so every reference outside this
॰ file must be written वाक्यविभागॱआज्ञा and never bare.
॰
॰ ── ON THE MODULE NAME ── पदविभाग is "word division" and is the lexer.
॰ वाक्यविभाग is "sentence division" and is this: T0's statement IS a
॰ sentence (doc 02 §2.2, ADR-0004 — a verb and its kāraka-marked operands,
॰ ending in ।), and what parse.rs does at top level is divide the token
॰ stream into them. व्याकर, the obvious word, is spent on the T1 parser.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAMES ── attested words from spec/lexicon.src.tsv wherever the
॰ lexicon has one: आज्ञा instruction, कारक operand-role, चिह्न label,
॰ कोष्ठकम् section, निर्देश directive, संज्ञा mnemonic, वैश्विकम् global,
॰ अष्टक byte, नाम name, मूल्य value, संख्यानम् count, स्थान address.
॰ व्याप्ति for Width is parse.rs's own word for it ("Operand width —
॰ व्याप्ति, extent") and is what diagnostic P23 says out loud, so it is
॰ taken from the original rather than coined. कार्यक्रम for Program is
॰ the spelling सङ्केतन already uses in कार्यक्रमसङ्केतनम्.
॰
॰ ── ON GROUPING ── spec/grammar-t1.ebnf freezes आरभ्य ॱ समाप्तम्,
॰ आदि ॱ इति and अङ्कः ॱ अन्तः and says out loud that OPERATORS AND THEIR
॰ PRECEDENCE ARE NOT FROZEN. Every order-dependent expression below is
॰ bracketed, as मध्यरूप and संयोजन both do, so the file means one thing
॰ under either eventual rule.
॰
॰ ── ON THE ARENAS ── Rust's Program holds six Vec. T1 has no growable
॰ collection, so this file adopts the convention व्याकर opened and मध्यरूप
॰ followed and invents nothing: a preallocated कोश, a module-level
॰ सूचकाङ्क that the appending routine advances BEFORE it writes, and a
॰ (first index, count) pair in the record that owns the run. ० is never a
॰ live entry and therefore means ABSENT — so Rust's Option<T> is a ० here,
॰ and Section's #[derive(Default)] = Text is NOT free: आरम्भः sets the
॰ current कोष्ठक to पाठकोष्ठकभेद explicitly, because ० would otherwise mean
॰ "no section" where Rust means "the text section".
॰
॰ ── ON RANGES ── T1 indexes one element (अङ्कः ॱ अन्तः) and has no
॰ sub-slice expression, so a routine that Rust gives a &str is given a
॰ slice plus two indices here. That is why अङ्कव्याप्तिः takes आरम्भ and
॰ सीमा rather than the digits themselves.
॰
॰ ── ON COMPARING TEXT ── two techniques, and the choice is not stylistic.
॰ A whole word is compared with an ADR-0017 literal (उक्तम् पाठ इति),
॰ which is what व्याकरॱमेलनम् does. A DIGIT is compared as its bytes,
॰ because the frozen string production is string = string_open ,
॰ { aksara_word | … } and ८ is a numeral, not an akṣara word — so
॰ उक्तम् ८ इति is outside the grammar even though today's lexer would
॰ take it. पदविभागॱविभज already compares a sigil as bytes; this is that.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS IN THIS FILE, ROW BY ROW ── D-002f1 was the RECORDS and the
॰ routines that need nothing but them, and it READ NO TOKEN. D-002f3
॰ landed the statement splitter, वाक्यविभाजनम्. D-002f5 landed the
॰ directive reader's first half, निर्देशानुष्ठानम् and its four arms. The
॰ sentence reader (D-002f4) and the directives that emit bytes (D-002f6,
॰ D-002f7) are still to come, and (b) at the foot says so exactly. The
॰ tests the_t0_reader_reports_whether_it_reads_any_token and
॰ the_directive_reader_applies_the_directives_that_emit_no_bytes exist so
॰ that a full symbol table and a full count of real bodies cannot be
॰ mistaken for a working reader — both were pinned at ० and both moved
॰ only when something was actually read. The two registry readers
॰ (families, directives) are blocked and named at the foot of this file.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

आयातः पदविभाग ।

॰ FOR THE TSV ROW-WALK HELPERS — `पङ्क्तिसीमा`, `उपेक्ष्यपङ्क्तिः`,
॰ `क्षेत्रसंख्या`, `क्षेत्रारम्भः`, `क्षेत्रसीमा`. This file ALREADY called them
॰ qualified at `:3206` and had no import for them, and `जालपङ्क्तिः` called the
॰ same five UNQUALIFIED — one file, one row walk, written two ways, and neither
॰ resolvable. `अर्थ` reports only its first refusal, so the unqualified copy
॰ masked the missing import behind it for as long as it stood.
॰
॰ THE CYCLE THIS COMPLETES ALREADY EXISTED: `सङ्केतन` imports `निदान`
॰ (encode.t1:26) and `निदान` imports `सङ्केतन` (nidana.t1:99). Mutual imports
॰ are the corpus's existing practice, not something introduced here.
आयातः सङ्केतन ।

॰ FOR THE EIGHT `अक्षरकोशॱ` CALLS AT `:3180`–`:3208` — `W-204`, 2026-09-04.
॰ Called qualified, never imported, and unseen by `अर्थ` because all eight
॰ sit inside one `अन्यथा` block and the resolver read a यदि's condition and
॰ then-body only (W-202 is the else-walk; W-204 met the same sites while
॰ making the IR refuse a callee with no symbol). The interpreter had reached
॰ across regardless, so nothing ran differently, and nothing said so — except
॰ `t1_modules.rs`, whose REACHED_WITHOUT_IMPORTING row carried these eight
॰ lines; that row is removed in the same commit, as its margin instructs.
आयातः अक्षरकोश ।

॰ W-239 (2026-09-04): THE OCTET ARENA — the store this file's own ASCII margin
॰ promised at (e) and the foot never wrote. `अष्टकसञ्चयः` and its two appenders
॰ were declared here for the width directives; they are now the module `अष्टक`
॰ (ashtaka.t1), completed with a text append, a range out, and a refusal.
॰ A datum's `अष्टकाः` is a range of that one arena.
आयातः अष्टक ।


॰ ══════════════════ sections ══════════════════
॰ enum Section. ० is not a section: it means ABSENT, so आरम्भः must set
॰ the current one rather than inherit Rust's #[derive(Default)].

सार्वजनिक चरः पाठकोष्ठकभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति १ ।    ॰ Section::Text  — ॱपाठ
सार्वजनिक चरः दत्तकोष्ठकभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति २ ।    ॰ Section::Data  — ॱदत्त
सार्वजनिक चरः रिक्तकोष्ठकभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ३ ।   ॰ Section::Bss   — ॱरिक्त


॰ ══════════════════ operand widths ══════════════════
॰ enum Width. The suffix ॱअ३२ selects among the encodings one family
॰ covers (R-02-2); W64 is what a bare mnemonic means.

सार्वजनिक चरः अष्टकव्याप्तिभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति १ ।       ॰ Width::W8
सार्वजनिक चरः षोडशव्याप्तिभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति २ ।        ॰ Width::W16
सार्वजनिक चरः द्वात्रिंशव्याप्तिभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ३ ।  ॰ Width::W32
सार्वजनिक चरः चतुःषष्टिव्याप्तिभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ४ ।   ॰ Width::W64


॰ ══════════════════ statement kinds ══════════════════
॰ enum StatementKind. A comment is absent here exactly as it is in Rust:
॰ पदविभाग strips from ॰ to end of line before this module is reached
॰ (B-067), so it is not a statement anything here can see.

सार्वजनिक चरः आज्ञावाक्यभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति १ ।      ॰ StatementKind::Instruction
सार्वजनिक चरः चिह्नवाक्यभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति २ ।      ॰ StatementKind::Label
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्देशवाक्यभेद ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ३ ।    ॰ StatementKind::Directive


॰ ══════════════════ one piece of text ══════════════════
॰ Rust writes Vec<String> three times — Family::covers, Program::globals
॰ and ParseError::args. T1 has no growable collection and no arena of
॰ slices, so each of the three is a RUN in one text arena, named by the
॰ (first index, count) pair in the record that owns it. One arena and not
॰ three because the runs are written contiguously by one appender and a
॰ second convention would have to be justified; मध्यरूप makes the same
॰ move for Rust's Vec<(ValueId, Instruction)>.

सार्वजनिक संरचना पाठांश आरभ्य
    पाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ         ॰ the text this piece lies IN
    आरम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                  ॰ first octet of the piece
    सीमा ॱॱ अ६४                     ॰ one past its last
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ one registry row ══════════════════
॰ struct Family, one row of spec/mnemonics-riscv64.src.tsv. R-02-1 says
॰ the ISA surface IS that file, so this record is the whole of what an
॰ instruction may be — and see (a) at the foot: nothing fills it yet.

सार्वजनिक संरचना संज्ञाकुल आरभ्य
    कूट ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ         ॰ key — the Latin family key, e.g. add
    नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ         ॰ name — the Devanagari mnemonic
    व्याख्या ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ     ॰ gloss
    विस्तारः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ     ॰ ext — I, M, A, FD, Zicsr, Zifencei
    आवरणारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ              ॰ covers: first index into पाठांशकोश
    आवरणसंख्यान ॱॱ अ६४              ॰ covers: how many
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ one operand ══════════════════
॰ struct Operand. कारक is the ROLE and is पदविभागॱविभज's answer — 1 कर्म,
॰ 2 करण, 3 अपादान, 4 सम्प्रदान, 5 अधिकरण, ० none — so this file does not
॰ restate the sigil table the lexer already owns.
॰
॰ NOTE FOR D-002f4: पदविभागॱचिह्नक carries भेद, पाठ, अष्टक, अक्षर and
॰ पङ्क्ति and NOT Rust's Kind::Operand { base, karaka }. The T1 token has
॰ no operand payload, so the reader that fills this record must call
॰ पदविभागॱविभज for the role and take the base by length. That is a
॰ finding about lex.t1, recorded here where it will be needed rather than
॰ discovered again.

सार्वजनिक संरचना कारकपद आरभ्य
    मूलपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ      ॰ base — the text with the sigil removed
    कारक ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                   ॰ karaka — पदविभाग's role number
    सङ्ख्यात्व ॱॱ बूल                ॰ is_numeral
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ one instruction ══════════════════
॰ struct Instruction. Rust's types: Vec<String> is at most TWO — one
॰ व्याप्ति for an ordinary instruction, two for a conversion (B-075) —
॰ so it is two fields and a count rather than an arena run. That is not
॰ the arena convention being abandoned; it is the Vec having a bound the
॰ Rust type does not write down but parse_statement enforces with P08.

सार्वजनिक संरचना आज्ञा आरभ्य
    कुल ॱॱ संज्ञाकुल ऽ              ॰ family — the registry row it resolved to
    व्याप्ति ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ               ॰ width — चतुःषष्टिव्याप्तिभेद by default
    प्रथमप्रकार ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ  ॰ types[0] — what it WRITES
    द्वितीयप्रकार ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ ॰ types[1] — what a conversion READS
    प्रकारसंख्यान ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ          ॰ types.len() — 0, 1 or 2
    कारकारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ              ॰ operands: first index into कारकपदकोश
    कारकसंख्यान ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ            ॰ operands: how many
    पङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४                  ॰ line
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ an address a datum names ══════════════════
॰ Rust's (usize, String) in Datum::addresses — ADR-0013. A datum stops
॰ being complete when it is parsed: eight bytes are reserved and left
॰ zero, and संयोजन fills them once every label has an address.

सार्वजनिक संरचना स्थाननिर्देश आरभ्य
    सरण ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                    ॰ byte offset into the datum's bytes
    नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८           ॰ the label whose address goes there
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ bytes a directive emitted ══════════════════
॰ struct Datum.

सार्वजनिक संरचना दत्तम् आरभ्य
    कोष्ठक ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                 ॰ section
    अष्टकाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ      ॰ bytes, little-endian, already widened
    स्थानारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ             ॰ addresses: first index
    स्थानसंख्यान ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ           ॰ addresses: how many
    पङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४                  ॰ line
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ a label definition ══════════════════
॰ struct Label. आज्ञाक्रम is an instruction INDEX and not an address:
॰ addresses belong to सङ्केतन, the only part that knows how many bytes an
॰ instruction takes, and B-007's relaxation fixpoint is exactly that
॰ answer changing as compressed forms are chosen.

सार्वजनिक संरचना चिह्न आरभ्य
    नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ         ॰ the source the name lies IN
    नामारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ               ॰ name: first octet, without the ॱॱ
    नामसीमा ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                ॰ name: one past its last
    कोष्ठक ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                 ॰ section it names a place in
    दत्तसरण ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                ॰ data_offset — bytes into that section
    आज्ञाक्रम ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ              ॰ at — index of the instruction it marks
    पङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४                  ॰ line
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ one statement, in written order ══════════════════
॰ struct Statement — the file's SHAPE rather than its content, which is
॰ what a second parser is checked against (B-034a). Three directives mean
॰ nothing storable — कोष्ठकम् changes a section, वैश्विकम् pushes a name,
॰ स्थानीयम् does nothing at all — so without this record a parser could
॰ drop all three unseen.

सार्वजनिक संरचना वाक्य आरभ्य
    भेद ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                    ॰ kind — one of the three above
    पङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                ॰ line
    नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ         ॰ the source the first word lies IN
    नामारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ               ॰ the first word: first octet
    नामसीमा ॱॱ अ६४                  ॰ the first word: one past its last
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ an alignment request in ॱपाठ ══════════════════
॰ Rust's (usize, usize) in Program::text_aligns. W-071: alignment in a
॰ text section cannot be resolved while parsing, for the same reason a
॰ branch's width cannot, so the REQUEST is recorded and स्थानविन्यासः
॰ satisfies it.

सार्वजनिक संरचना संरेख आरभ्य
    आज्ञाक्रम ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ              ॰ the instruction the padding sits before
    सीमा ॱॱ अ६४                     ॰ the boundary n
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ one directive of the registry ══════════════════
॰ struct DirectiveKind, one row of spec/directives.tsv — and see (a).
॰
॰ EACH OF THE THREE GAINED A RANGE IN D-002f5, and for the reason D-002f3
॰ gave when वाक्य ॱ नाम, चिह्न ॱ नाम and पाठांश ॱ पाठ gained theirs: a row
॰ of a table is a RANGE IN THE EMBEDDED FILE and T1 has no sub-slice
॰ expression, so a bare अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ per column is a field the registry
॰ reader could never fill. Written as three columns of whole text this
॰ record was unfillable and therefore P13 and P14 were unreachable —
॰ निर्देशान्वेषणम् below compares against नामारम्भ ॱ नामसीमा and
॰ असमर्थितनिर्देशः reads यवनारम्भ ॱ यवनसीमा for P14's second argument. It
॰ is an EXTENSION and not an alteration: no field lost a name or a type.

सार्वजनिक संरचना निर्देश आरभ्य
    नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ         ॰ the text the Devanagari name lies IN
    नामारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ               ॰ name: first octet
    नामसीमा ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                ॰ name: one past its last
    यवननाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ      ॰ gas — what another assembler calls it
    यवनारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ               ॰ gas: first octet
    यवनसीमा ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ                ॰ gas: one past its last
    स्थिति ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ       ॰ status — live or planned
    स्थित्यारम्भ ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ            ॰ status: first octet
    स्थितिसीमा ॱॱ अ६४               ॰ status: one past its last
समाप्तम् ।


