॰ the section currently open, and the two Program fields that are counted
॰ rather than collected. Rust keeps `section` as a local of parse(); here
॰ it is module state for the same reason व्याकर keeps पठनस्थान module
॰ state — T1 has no &mut parameter.
सार्वजनिक चरः वर्तमानकोष्ठक ॱॱ अ६४ भवति १ ।
सार्वजनिक चरः रिक्तमानम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः रिक्तपङ्क्तिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ Rust's Program::globals. D-002f1 made this a RUN IN पाठांशकोश, on the
॰ ground that a global is one piece of text and पाठांशकोश is where a piece
॰ of text goes — and D-002f5, WRITING THE FIRST GLOBAL, MEASURED THAT TO
॰ BE WRONG AND GIVES IT ITS OWN ARENA.
॰
॰ The reason is that पाठांशकोश is not this run's alone: every diagnostic
॰ pushes its args there too, and the walk raises diagnostics BETWEEN two
॰ directives. So `॥ वैश्विकम् क ॥`, then anything that reports (a bare `॥`
॰ raises P24), then `॥ वैश्विकम् ख ॥` leaves पाठांशकोश holding क, the P24
॰ argument and ख — three entries — while वैश्विकसंख्यानम् is २. The run
॰ then names क and the P24 argument, and वैश्विकचिह्नपरीक्षा reports L02
॰ against a word that was never a global. A run is only a run while ONE
॰ appender writes the arena; that is the convention's precondition and it
॰ is stated here because it was found by breaking it, not by reading it.
॰
॰ पाठांशयोजनम् is untouched and still Rust's Vec<String> push: Family ॱ
॰ covers and ParseError ॱ args are both still runs in पाठांशकोश, and both
॰ ARE written by one appender each within one record's construction.
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विककोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः पाठांश भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकारम्भः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति १ ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकसंख्यानम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।


॰ ══════════════════ Program::default ══════════════════
॰ Rust gets an empty Program from #[derive(Default)] and a Text section
॰ from Section's own. Here both are this routine, and the section is set
॰ EXPLICITLY: ० means absent everywhere else in this file, so a zeroed
॰ वर्तमानकोष्ठक would mean "no section open" where Rust means ॱपाठ.

