॰ ══════════════════ Section::from_name ══════════════════
॰ The name as written, without the ॱ — which पदविभाग has already stripped
॰ by the time a directive's argument is a token's पाठ. ० is None, and a
॰ name that is none of the three is refused rather than defaulted: P15
॰ exists because a mistyped section is a program that assembles into the
॰ wrong place and says nothing.

॰ IT TAKES A RANGE, AND D-002f5 IS WHY. D-002f1 wrote it against a whole
॰ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८, which is what Rust's &str is; but the only caller there
॰ will ever be is the कोष्ठकम् arm, and what that arm holds is a TOKEN —
॰ पाठ plus अष्टक plus पाठसीमा, a range in the source, because T1 has no
॰ sub-slice expression to cut the name out with. Written against whole
॰ text this routine was not callable at all. Same EXTENSION as the three
॰ records D-002f3 gave ranges to, and it loses nothing: पाठसाम्यम् over
॰ [० ऽ दैर्घ्य) is the whole-text comparison the old body made.

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः कोष्ठकनाम आदाय नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ नामारम्भः ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ नामसीमा ॱॱ अ६४ ददाति अ६४ आदि
    ॰ W-239 (2026-09-04): THE OPERAND CARRIES ITS MARK. A section is written
    ॰ `ॱदत्त`, and the T1 lexer keeps the single `ॱ` inside the word (lex.t1:
    ॰ "ॱ IS NOT AMONG" the peelable signs), so the operand token's text is
    ॰ `ॱदत्त`; Rust's arm compares against "ॱदत्त" and this one compared against
    ॰ "दत्त" — every section directive a T1 program wrote was P15. The mark
    ॰ (U+0971, octets २२४ १६५ १७७) is stepped over before the names are tried.
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति नामारम्भः ।
    यदि आरभ्य आरम्भः योगः ३ समाप्तम् न्यूनम् नामसीमा आदि
        यदि नाम अङ्कः आरम्भः अन्तः समम् २२४ आदि
            यदि नाम अङ्कः आरभ्य आरम्भः योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः समम् १६५ आदि
                यदि नाम अङ्कः आरभ्य आरम्भः योगः २ समाप्तम् अन्तः समम् १७७ आदि
                    आरम्भः भवति आरम्भः योगः ३ ।
                इति
            इति
        इति
    इति
    चरः पाठसंज्ञा ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् पाठ इति ।
    यदि पाठसाम्यम् आरभ्य नाम ऽ आरम्भः ऽ नामसीमा ऽ पाठसंज्ञा ऽ ० ऽ पाठसंज्ञा ॱ दैर्घ्य समाप्तम् आदि
