॰ ══════════════════ StatementKind::as_str — BLOCKED ══════════════════
॰ Rust returns "instruction", "label" or "directive": the words
॰ spec/parse-shape-t0.tsv is written in, and they are LATIN. Doc 15's
॰ repertoire refuses a Latin letter and ADR-0017 is blunt that a string
॰ literal is not a licence to smuggle one back in — "a Latin letter inside
॰ a string is refused exactly as it is anywhere else". So this routine
॰ cannot be written, and the decision it waits on is not code: either
॰ spec/parse-shape-t0.tsv gains a Devanagari column, or the shape oracle
॰ compares भेद numbers instead of words. It is the same blocker that holds
॰ four of उत्सर्जन's seven emitters, and it is stubbed rather than
॰ approximated for the same reason.

॰ WRITTEN 2026-08-30, AND NO SPEC TABLE WAS NEEDED. The recorded blocker
॰ asked for "spec/parse-shape-t0.tsv gains a Devanagari column, or the shape
॰ oracle compares भेद numbers instead of words". BOTH HALVES ARE ABOUT THE
॰ ORACLE'S COMPARISON, not about this routine: parse-shape-t0.tsv is a
॰ GENERATED golden of 9502 rows recording one parse per line, and a column
॰ there would be a per-row copy of a three-valued fact.
॰
