॰ the seven D-002f5 raises, on the same terms. Six are codes; जीवत्पाठः is
॰ the STATUS WORD of spec/directives.tsv, and it is here for exactly the
॰ reason the codes are — `live` is Latin, doc 15's repertoire refuses a
॰ Latin letter, and ADR-0017 is blunt that a string literal is not a
॰ licence to smuggle one back in. So the word a live directive carries can
॰ only exist in a T1 source as its octets: 'l' १०८, 'i' १०५, 'v' ११८,
॰ 'e' १०१. THIS IS A FINDING ABOUT spec/directives.tsv AND NOT A
॰ WORKAROUND — the status column is Latin in a file every tier reads, and
॰ P14 cannot be raised without comparing against it.
