॰ the three radix prefixes of sanskrit_text::numeral, as octets — and NOT
॰ as ADR-0017 literals, for the reason this file's header gives at ON
॰ COMPARING TEXT: each begins with ०, ० is a NUMERAL and not an akṣara
॰ word, and the frozen string production admits akṣara words. `उक्तम् ०द्वि
॰ इति` is outside the grammar even though today's lexer would take it.
॰ ऋण by contrast is two letters and IS written as a literal, at ऋणचिह्नम्.
