॰ WHAT IS NOT PORTED, AND WHY. Two blockers and four rows.
॰
॰ (a) THE TWO REGISTRY READERS — families() and directives() — read
॰ spec/mnemonics-riscv64.src.tsv and spec/directives.tsv through
॰ include_str!. THE OLD SENTENCE HERE SAID "T1 HAS NO FILE READER" AND
॰ D-002f5 MEASURED THAT TO BE STALE: ADR-0019 landed the embed on
॰ 2026-08-28 (D-002g), `समावेशः आरभ्य <name> समाप्तम्`, and encode.t1 and
॰ samyojana.t1 both use it today. What is actually missing is smaller and
॰ exact: the embed resolves an IDENTIFIER against TABLES in
॰ crates/sadhana/src/t1/anita.rs, and NEITHER spec/directives.tsv NOR
॰ spec/mnemonics-riscv64.src.tsv is quite reachable — mnemonics IS listed,
॰ as नामकोशः, but directives.tsv HAS NO NAME THERE AT ALL, so it is
॰ unreachable however much it exists on disk. That is one line of Rust and
॰ it is D-002f2's to add, exactly as D-002i2 had संस्कारकोशः added for it.
॰ Neither reader is stubbed here: a stub says "unwritten", and what is
॰ true is that the file cannot be named. संज्ञाकुलयोजनम् and
॰ निर्देशयोजनम् are the per-row halves of both and are written and real,
॰ and D-002f5 added निर्देशान्वेषणम् and जीवन्निर्देशः above them, so the
॰ remaining work is a loop and not a record. Nothing here hand-copies a
॰ derived table: a typed second copy agrees with the first by construction
॰ and checks nothing.
॰
॰ (b) THE TOKEN LOOP IS READ, AND SO IS ONE OF THE TWO READERS UNDER IT.
॰ D-002f3 landed वाक्यविभाजनम् above — parse.rs:485-612's `for tok in
॰ tokens` plus its three post-checks — so this file READS पदविभागॱचिह्नक
॰ and वाक्यविभागवाक्यकोश fills from real input. D-002f5 landed निर्देशानुष्ठानम्,
॰ apply_directive's first half, so a paired ॥ … ॥ now CHANGES SECTION,
॰ EXPORTS A NAME and ALIGNS, and वैश्विकचिह्नपरीक्षा's L02 loop has
॰ something to read. What is still absent is parse_statement, which turns
॰ a statement's run into an आज्ञा (D-002f4) — so after a walk वाक्यविभागआज्ञाकोश is
॰ still empty — and apply_directive's SECOND half, the directives that
॰ emit bytes (D-002f6) and the text ones (D-002f7). A directive of those
॰ two rows is not refused here: the registry has already said the word IS
॰ a directive, and refusing it again would report a fault in the source
॰ for a gap in the port. That is stated at निर्देशानुष्ठानम् too.
॰
॰ (c) THAT SECOND ABSENCE IS CLOSED. पदविभागॱपदविभाग wrote NOTHING into
॰ चिह्नककोश when this file was written, so even a finished reader would
॰ have read an empty arena; D-002f10 landed the lexer (121 -> 502 lines,
॰ two append sites, six kinds produced) and the arena is real. TWO OF ITS
॰ FIVE RECORDED LIMITS REACH THIS FILE and are not re-measured here:
॰ अक्षर IS A CODE-POINT INDEX and not an akṣara index (अक्षरकोश ॱ अक्षराणि
॰ is a stub), so every diagnostic placed above inherits that; and
॰ सङ्ख्याभेद IS NEVER PRODUCED, so a numeral lexes as पदभेद — which the
॰ splitter does not care about, every non-delimiter kind extending the
॰ statement alike, but D-002f4 will.
॰
॰ (d) nearest()/distance() — the akṣara-level edit distance behind "did
॰ you mean" — needs sanskrit_text::aksharas, akṣara segmentation, which
॰ no .t1 module has. It is its own row and its own port.
