॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE DIRECTIVES THAT EMIT BYTES — D-002f6, parse.rs:857-1009.
॰
॰ स्थानम् / अष्टकाः / द्वयष्टकाः / चतुरष्टकाः / अष्टाष्टकाः: one Rust match
॰ arm over five names, and the five are one arm because they differ only
॰ in HOW WIDE the destination is. `let width = match head.text` is
॰ निर्देशव्याप्तिः below; the pattern list itself is अष्टकनिर्देशवाचकः,
॰ which is what lets the ॥…॥ arm reach this half without the registry
॰ lookup and the four non-emitting arms that are D-002f5's row.
॰
॰ ── TWO READERS FOR TWO QUESTIONS — W-075 ──
॰ A DATUM IS A BIT PATTERN and A COUNT IS A MAGNITUDE, and one reader
॰ answering both is how a literal too large became i64::MAX and was
॰ emitted as one. So ॥ अष्टाष्टकाः ऋण१ ॥ is eight octets of ones and
॰ ॥ स्थानम् ऋण५ ॥ is P30 and not a request to reserve 0xffff…fb bytes of
॰ address space. The two readers are अक्षरकोश ॱ मानम् (numeral::value)
॰ and अक्षरकोश ॱ अंशाः (numeral::bits), each paired with the routine that
॰ answers its fault, because Rust returns a Result and T1 has no tuple.
॰
॰ THOSE FOUR ARE STUBS TODAY and this port says so rather than hiding it.
॰ numeral.rs is radix prefixes, digit values and checked arithmetic and
॰ it is अक्षरकोश's to own — मध्यरूप ॱ अङ्कमूल्यम् gives the reason for
॰ calling a stub there rather than transcribing the module a second time,
॰ and the same reason holds here. WHAT IS NOT BLOCKED BY IT is everything
॰ around them: the width table, the fit check, the two-reader SPLIT, the
॰ address placeholder, and the section rules, all of which are written.
॰ When the four land, ॥ अष्टकाः ३०० ॥ raises P31 with no edit here.
॰
॰ ── THE FIT CHECK REFUSES RATHER THAN TRUNCATES — W-082 ──
॰ ॥ अष्टकाः ३०० ॥ used to emit ०षोड्२च silently. GNU as warns and
॰ truncates; THIS TOOLCHAIN HAS NO WARNING CHANNEL, and R-02-1's stance
॰ is emit-what-was-written-or-refuse, so the only answer that keeps what
॰ was written and what was emitted the same number is to refuse.
॰
॰ ── A NAME IS AN ADDRESS — ADR-0013 ──
॰ A token that begins with a digit or a radix prefix is a numeral; one
॰ that begins with a letter is a NAME, and a name is the address of what
॰ it names. Eight zero octets are reserved and स्थाननिर्देशयोजनम् records
॰ the fixup, which संयोजन fills once every label has an address.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE ──
॰ (1) The string branch — args.first() == उक्तम्, string_body, P17, P18,
॰     P22 — is D-002f7 (THE TEXT DIRECTIVES), together with आस्की and
॰     जाल. This routine DECLINES a उक्तम् statement rather than falling
॰     through to the operand loop, because falling through would read
॰     उक्तम् as a label name and reserve eight octets for it. An absence
॰     that is visible beats one that assembles.
॰ (2) Rust's usize::try_from(v) for स्थानम् has nothing to port: it
॰     narrows u64 to usize, and अ६४ IS the count type here, so the
॰     conversion is the identity and a check on it would test nothing.
॰     The P29 that CAN fire is the reader's own, below.
॰ (3) The octet arena is NOT rewound when a later operand raises. Rust
॰     drops a local Vec; here the run stays in अष्टकसञ्चयः with no दत्तम्
॰     naming it, so the program is right and the arena holds unreferenced
॰     octets. Stated rather than left to be found.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

॰ a token's whole text against a literal — Rust's head.text == "…".
॰ पाठसाम्यम् with the literal's own range, which is the shape
॰ वैश्विकपङ्क्तिः already uses for उक्तम् वैश्विकम् इति.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः चिह्नकनामसाम्यम् आदाय चिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक ऽ अपेक्षितम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति बूल आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् पाठसाम्यम् आरभ्य चिह्नकम् ॱ पाठ ऽ चिह्नकम् ॱ अष्टक ऽ चिह्नकम् ॱ पाठसीमा ऽ अपेक्षितम् ऽ ० ऽ अपेक्षितम् ॱ दैर्घ्य समाप्तम् ।
इति


॰ the match arm's own PATTERN LIST — the five names this half is for.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः अष्टकनिर्देशवाचकः आदाय शिरःचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक ददाति बूल आदि
    यदि चिह्नकनामसाम्यम् आरभ्य शिरःचिह्नकम् ऽ उक्तम् स्थानम् इति समाप्तम् आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि चिह्नकनामसाम्यम् आरभ्य शिरःचिह्नकम् ऽ उक्तम् अष्टकाः इति समाप्तम् आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि चिह्नकनामसाम्यम् आरभ्य शिरःचिह्नकम् ऽ उक्तम् द्वयष्टकाः इति समाप्तम् आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि चिह्नकनामसाम्यम् आरभ्य शिरःचिह्नकम् ऽ उक्तम् चतुरष्टकाः इति समाप्तम् आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि चिह्नकनामसाम्यम् आरभ्य शिरःचिह्नकम् ऽ उक्तम् अष्टाष्टकाः इति समाप्तम् आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
इति


