    ॰ P28 — ॱपाठ holds INSTRUCTIONS. A data directive written there used
    ॰ to put its octets in ॱदत्त, a section the author never named, while
    ॰ any label around it kept naming the NEXT INSTRUCTION — so two labels
    ॰ either side of it compared equal and reading through one returned an
    ॰ opcode octet (W-071, found from the other side by E-004). Refused
    ॰ rather than placed, because placing it needs ॱपाठ to address octets
    ॰ instead of instructions, which is a change to how the section is
    ॰ modelled and not to this directive.
    यदि वर्तमानकोष्ठक समम् पाठकोष्ठकभेद आदि
        चरः शिरःपदार्थः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति चिह्नकपदार्थः शिरःचिह्नकम् ।
